{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>One he-goat for a sin-offering.</b> There was no need to write 'to make atonement for you,' for this day is a day of completion of atonement." "<b>Besides the sin-offering of atonement.</b> Rashi's comment: the goat made inside, mentioned in the section of אחרי מות, which is also a sin-offering. But one may answer: it does not count it here among the offerings brought from public funds, for the bull made inside — which is Aaron's bull — does not come from public funds but from Aaron's own." "<b>And their drink-offerings.</b> This refers to the wine drink-offerings of the Day of Atonement, and to the wine drink-offerings and the meal-offerings of the daily burnt-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:12.030562136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}